    We collect limited information necessary to provide app functionality, maintain user preferences, and display advertisements. We do not sell your personal information to third parties.
</div>

<h2>Our Apps</h2>

<p>This Privacy Policy applies to all mobile applications published by TinySpark Apps, including:</p>

<ul>
    <li><strong>Baby Names with Meaning</strong></li>
    <li>Any future applications released under the TinySpark Apps developer account</li>
</ul>

<h2>1. Information We Collect</h2>

<h3>Information You Provide</h3>

<p>You may voluntarily provide the following information when using our applications:</p>

<ul>
    <li>Email Address</li>
    <li>Phone Number</li>
</ul>

<h3>Automatically Collected Information</h3>

<p>Our applications may automatically collect certain technical information, including:</p>

<ul>
    <li>Unique Device Identifier generated by the application</li>
    <li>Application Version</li>
    <li>Account Creation Timestamp</li>
    <li>Advertising and diagnostic information collected by third-party services</li>
</ul>

<h3>Information Stored Locally on Your Device</h3>

<p>The following information is stored locally on your device and is not uploaded to our servers:</p>

<ul>
    <li>Favorite baby names</li>
    <li>Recently viewed names</li>
    <li>App preferences and settings</li>
    <li>Tutorial completion status</li>
    <li>Review prompt counters</li>
</ul>

<h2>2. How We Use Information</h2>

<p>We use collected information to:</p>

<ul>
    <li>Provide app functionality and services</li>
    <li>Maintain user preferences and records</li>
    <li>Improve app stability and performance</li>
    <li>Display advertisements</li>
    <li>Detect fraud, abuse, and technical issues</li>
    <li>Comply with legal obligations</li>
    <li>Provide customer support when requested</li>
</ul>

<h2>3. Third-Party Services</h2>

<p>Our apps use third-party services that may collect and process information according to their own privacy policies.</p>

<ul>
    <li>
        <strong>Google Firebase</strong><br>
        Used for storing user information and application-related data.
    </li>

    <li>
        <strong>Google Mobile Ads (AdMob)</strong><br>
        Used to display advertisements. AdMob may collect device identifiers, advertising identifiers, IP address information, app interaction information, and diagnostic information for advertising and fraud prevention purposes.
    </li>

    <li>
        <strong>Google Play Services</strong><br>
        Used for app distribution, updates, reviews, and platform functionality.
    </li>
</ul>

<h2>4. Data Storage and Security</h2>

<ul>
    <li>User information submitted through the application may be stored securely using Google Firebase services.</li>
    <li>Locally stored app data remains on your device unless removed by you or deleted when the app is uninstalled.</li>
    <li>We implement reasonable security measures to protect information from unauthorized access, disclosure, alteration, or destruction.</li>
    <li>We do not sell personal information to third parties.</li>
</ul>

<h2>5. Your Rights</h2>

<p>Depending on your jurisdiction, you may have rights regarding your personal information, including:</p>

<ul>
    <li>Request access to your information</li>
    <li>Request correction of inaccurate information</li>
    <li>Request deletion of your information</li>
    <li>Withdraw consent where applicable</li>
</ul>

<p>To exercise any of these rights, please contact us using the details below.</p>

<h2>6. Children's Privacy</h2>

<p>
    Our applications are intended for general audiences, including parents researching baby names.
    We do not knowingly collect personal information from children under the age of 13.
    If you believe a child has provided personal information to us, please contact us so that appropriate action can be taken.
</p>

